> On Sat, Jun 19, 2004 at 07:57:21PM -0700, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> > A different case (simplified):
> > 
> >     broda sei abu to broda
> > 
> > Again, jbofihe and the official parser choke on this.
> 
> Ah, I see the problem: sei can't contain to...toi, so the sei has no
> selbri.
> 
> xorxes, that's a bug in Alice.

Oh, no, my bad.

A SEI clause is (in PEG):

SEI free* (terms (CU free*)?)? selbri SEhU?

One of the options for 'free' is a TO clause, so it works out just fine
in the end.  That kind of look-ahead can't be done it LR(1), though.

